    "body": "Just came new to Starship and was very surprised by this.\r\n\r\nCurrently, there are about ~65 modules of which ~55 are enabled by default. I want maybe 5 and I'm guessing most users aren't that different.\r\n\r\nIt seems Starship expects users to either go all in or manually maintain a config file with ~55 entries with `[module] disabled = true` that they then also have to keep expanding as Starship adds new modules that are again enabled by default...\r\n\r\nI think this is the wrong approach. Modules should be disabled by default. Change the `disabled` option into `enabled` and at most put a few `[module] enabled = true` into the config for Git and co. that the user can simply delete.\r\n\r\nHere's the full output of `starship print-config` formatted with Nushell. Ignore the rows with an empty value which couldn't be filtered due to https://github.com/nushell/nushell/issues/4094.\r\n\r\n`> starship print-config | from toml | pivot | select Column0 Column1.disabled | rename \"Module\" \"Disabled\"`\r\n\r\n```\r\n────┬─────────────────┬──────────\r\n #  │     Module      │ Disabled \r\n────┼─────────────────┼──────────\r\n  0 │ add_newline     │          \r\n  1 │ command_timeout │          \r\n  2 │ format          │          \r\n  3 │ right_format    │          \r\n  4 │ scan_timeout    │          \r\n  5 │ aws             │ false    \r\n  6 │ battery         │ false    \r\n  7 │ character       │ false    \r\n  8 │ cmake           │ false    \r\n  9 │ cmd_duration    │ false     \r\n 10 │ cobol           │ false    \r\n 11 │ conda           │ false    \r\n 12 │ crystal         │ false    \r\n 13 │ custom          │          \r\n 14 │ dart            │ false    \r\n 15 │ deno            │ false    \r\n 16 │ directory       │ false    \r\n 17 │ docker_context  │ false    \r\n 18 │ dotnet          │ false    \r\n 19 │ elixir          │ false    \r\n 20 │ elm             │ false    \r\n 21 │ env_var         │          \r\n 22 │ erlang          │ false    \r\n 23 │ fill            │          \r\n 24 │ gcloud          │ false    \r\n 25 │ git_branch      │ false    \r\n 26 │ git_commit      │ false    \r\n 27 │ git_metrics     │ true     \r\n 28 │ git_state       │ false    \r\n 29 │ git_status      │ false    \r\n 30 │ golang          │ false    \r\n 31 │ helm            │ false    \r\n 32 │ hg_branch       │ true     \r\n 33 │ hostname        │ false    \r\n 34 │ java            │ false    \r\n 35 │ jobs            │ false    \r\n 36 │ julia           │ false    \r\n 37 │ kotlin          │ false    \r\n 38 │ kubernetes      │ true     \r\n 39 │ line_break      │ false    \r\n 40 │ lua             │ false    \r\n 41 │ memory_usage    │ true     \r\n 42 │ nim             │ false    \r\n 43 │ nix_shell       │ false    \r\n 44 │ nodejs          │ false    \r\n 45 │ ocaml           │ false    \r\n 46 │ openstack       │ false    \r\n 47 │ package         │ false    \r\n 48 │ perl            │ false    \r\n 49 │ php             │ false    \r\n 50 │ purescript      │ false    \r\n 51 │ python          │ false    \r\n 52 │ red             │ false    \r\n 53 │ rlang           │ false    \r\n 54 │ ruby            │ false    \r\n 55 │ rust            │ false    \r\n 56 │ scala           │ false    \r\n 57 │ shell           │ true     \r\n 58 │ shlvl           │ true     \r\n 59 │ singularity     │ false    \r\n 60 │ status          │ true     \r\n 61 │ swift           │ false    \r\n 62 │ terraform       │ false    \r\n 63 │ time            │ true     \r\n 64 │ username        │ false    \r\n 65 │ vagrant         │ false    \r\n 66 │ vcsh            │ false    \r\n 67 │ vlang           │ false    \r\n 68 │ zig             │ false    \r\n────┴─────────────────┴──────────\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
